{
  "title": "About New Plugin",
  "plugin": "new",
  "story": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "og3wn3fj",
      "text": "The New plugin owns the experience of making NEW things on a wiki. Two jobs: it curates the plugin picker by skill level, and it supersedes the built-in Future ghost \u2014 the \"We could not find this page\" placeholder \u2014 adding similar-page search to every missing page."
    },
    {
      "type": "new",
      "id": "v3gtuz4c",
      "text": "LEVEL NUBE\nParagraph\nMarkdown\nImage\nVideo\nReference\n\nLEVEL AUTHOR\nParagraph\nMarkdown\nImage\nVideo\nReference\nCode\nHTML\nDate\nTimeline\nFamily\n\nLEVEL EXPERT\nALL\n\nLEVEL GEEK\nALL\n\nHIDE\nMath\nTransport\nRostermatic\nMech\nSolo\nUser Access Tokens"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "ipvrtpq9",
      "text": "## DSL"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gnr8imi0",
      "text": "Each `LEVEL` block names a skill tier and lists the plugins available at that tier \u2014 one plugin name per line, matching the name in its `factory.json`. `ALL` means every installed plugin. The `HIDE` block removes plugins from all levels regardless of tier. A `FACTORY classic|list|rollover` line pins the factory display style."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "d1dbda2f18742b65",
      "text": "## Factory Style\n\nThe factory item \u2014 the picker you get from the [+] button \u2014 can wear three skins. **Classic** (the default) is the untouched default-wiki menu. **List** is a searchable directory: each plugin a plain link with a 2-3 line summary beneath it. **Rollover** mirrors this plugin's own display \u2014 tabbed category sections of pill buttons, with a small-print panel at the foot that fills with a plugin's summary as you roll over its pill; click to choose.\n\nThe summaries are each plugin's own words \u2014 the first paragraph of its about page, shortened at a word boundary and cached for a day. Switch styles with the *Factory style* buttons on any `new` item, or pin one with a `FACTORY classic|list|rollover` line in the DSL; the choice persists in this browser and repaints on-screen factories immediately. The skins live in wiki-ux \u2014 on a farm without it, Classic is all there is."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "u58mcrci",
      "text": "LEVEL NUBE\nParagraph\nMarkdown\nImage\nVideo"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "cemjfu4i",
      "text": "LEVEL GEEK\nALL\n\nHIDE\nMath\nTransport"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xto57b09",
      "text": "Levels: `NUBE` \u2014 newcomer basics. `AUTHOR` \u2014 content creator. `EXPERT` \u2014 most plugins. `GEEK` \u2014 everything (minus HIDE list). The active level is stored in `localStorage` so it survives page navigation. A browser starts on `AUTHOR`; when the item does not define the active level, the nearest defined level below it applies (else the nearest above), and only the levels the item defines get a button. So an item with just `NUBE` and `GEEK` gives a newcomer the `NUBE` menu straight away."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "e8eed31576dcd65c",
      "text": "## The Future Ghost"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "354819d646d0d5e8",
      "text": "When a page is missing, wiki-client builds a `future` item. This plugin replaces that item's renderer at runtime: the original affordances survive untouched \u2014 the create button, template offers, transporter, neighborhood duplicates \u2014 and an *edge section* is appended: the five nearest pages by meaning to the missing title, plus **Search farm** and **Search federation** buttons that open a full ranked report as a ghost page. On a farm without the [[About Similarity Plugin]] server the probe fails once and the ghost passes through unchanged."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "a1005b32fa077c47",
      "text": "Why the runtime replacement? The wiki-client bundle preloads `window.plugins.future` and the plugin loader short-circuits on that map \u2014 a plugin literally *named* `future` can never load; `/plugins/future/future.js` is never fetched. The supported path is reassigning `window.plugins.future` from a client script that is already loaded, which is why this plugin's `factory.json` carries `\"editor\": true` \u2014 the preload flag that makes the wiki import this client at startup. Items rendered before the script lands are retro-fitted by an idempotent sweep."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "r1vqmrlt",
      "text": "## Repositories"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jiyqotb0",
      "text": "Source: [github.com/Hitchhikers-Guide-to-the-Galaxy/wiki-plugin-new](https://github.com/Hitchhikers-Guide-to-the-Galaxy/wiki-plugin-new)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "o67ozpvq",
      "text": "Package: [npmjs.com/package/wiki-plugin-new](https://www.npmjs.com/package/wiki-plugin-new)"
    }
  ],
